"20260806154815179784_459b1f8c"], "reason": "Evans's Journal of Hellenic 
Studies account associates the relevant gold-ring treasure, including the 
object later called the Ring of Nestor, with a Mycenaean rock-cut chamber tomb 
near Thisbê and reports discovery by a peasant near Dombrena. The source does 
not provide independent excavation confirmation or a precise chamber 
identification."}, {"criterion": "The evidence traces ownership and publication
history from the reported 1924 discovery or acquisition to Arthur Evans and 
identifies any documented provenance gaps.", "status": "unmet", 
