into cyclopentanone-derived molecules. In Figure 7, either ‘B’ or ‘D’ passes 
through hydration and then a Piancatelli rearrangement, which is usually an 
acid-catalyzed reaction carried out in aqueous-phase media. The proposed 
intermediary may explain the conversion from furan rings into 
cyclopentanone-derived molecules (H, and I). Furthermore, the final product in 
