'bundle_token': 'b3-ae445b01', 'content': 'The Ring of Nestor is identified in 
the supplied scholarly discussion as a gold signet ring and as CMS VI, no. 
277.[1] The available evidence supports a broad description of a gold ring with
a decorated bezel, but it does not provide authoritative measurements, a 
complete catalogue-style account of the hoop and bezel, or a specified 
manufacturing or surface-decoration technique for no. 277.[2] A measurement of 
